1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,620
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:05,040
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,110
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,360
I've been an emergency
room doctor

5
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,740
for twenty-four years.

6
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:12,290
Long shifts in a busy ER,

7
00:00:12,290 --> 00:00:14,420
on my feet the whole
shift,

8
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:16,510
kneeling next to patients
on stretchers

9
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:17,660
and on the floor

10
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,810
more times than I could
ever count.

11
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,110
That's a lot of years

12
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:22,450
on a pair of knees.

13
00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:23,590
I had my right knee

14
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:25,210
replaced two years ago.

15
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,040
It has hurt every day
since.

16
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,410
Not surgery pain.

17
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:29,620
I know what that felt
like,

18
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:30,460
and it went away.

19
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,610
This is different.

20
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:32,440
Tight.

21
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,220
Full.

22
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,350
Like a band around

23
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:36,100
the joint that never
loosens.

24
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:37,340
And for two years

25
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,830
I've been told the same
thing.

26
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:39,880
Give it time.

27
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:41,550
At six weeks it was
swelling,

28
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:42,810
and swelling is normal.

29
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:43,850
At three months,

30
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:44,930
give it six.

31
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:45,710
At six months,

32
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:47,270
some knees take a full
year.

33
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:48,020
At a year,

34
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:49,910
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

35
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:51,660
And I didn't just wait.

36
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:53,510
We went down the list.

37
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:54,900
More physical therapy.

38
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:55,810
Every session,

39
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:57,300
every exercise at home.

40
00:00:57,460 --> 00:00:58,600
I got stronger.

41
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:00,160
The tightness never moved.

42
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,630
The pain pills helped,

43
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:02,860
and that was the problem.

44
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,990
I'm already on enough
every morning,

45
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:05,960
and nobody could tell me

46
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:07,180
when I'd get to stop.

47
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:08,660
Then a nerve block.

48
00:01:08,710 --> 00:01:10,390
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

49
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:11,730
And after that, a second

50
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:12,810
operation to go back

51
00:01:12,810 --> 00:01:14,240
in and do it over.

52
00:01:14,410 --> 00:01:15,330
I said no.

53
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:17,590
Every morning I pulled on
my scrubs

54
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:18,580
and my knee felt like

55
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:20,540
a band was wrapped around
it,

56
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:23,090
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

57
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:24,660
Every morning I took
something

58
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:25,660
for it and went

59
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:26,630
in for my shift.

60
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:28,250
Couldn't do the stairs,

61
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:29,330
couldn't stand at the
counter

62
00:01:29,330 --> 00:01:30,880
long enough to finish
dinner,

63
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:32,410
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

64
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:34,650
game without shifting
every two minutes.

65
00:01:34,770 --> 00:01:36,260
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,630
and it turned ordinary
things,

67
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:40,260
like getting in the car

68
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:41,810
or up off the couch,

69
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:42,890
into a decision.

70
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:44,260
After a long and serious

71
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:45,580
talk with my wife,

72
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,400
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:48,950
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:50,690
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,530
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:54,940
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,700
No loosening, no
infection,

78
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:57,490
nothing wrong.

79
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,570
Only this time there

80
00:01:58,570 --> 00:01:59,770
was no new number.

81
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:01,040
Nobody said

82
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,260
give it another six
months.

83
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,940
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:04,980
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:05,920
lot for a while.

86
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:07,520
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:09,030
Then explain this.

88
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:11,230
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:11,230 --> 00:02:12,690
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:12,730 --> 00:02:14,640
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,220
I'd just come home from a
late

92
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,700
shift in the ER.

93
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,660
Everyone in the house was
asleep

94
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,450
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

95
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:22,520
with my leg up,

96
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,260
trying to find any angle
where

97
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:25,430
it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,890
was wrapped around my knee

99
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:27,770
and tightening.

100
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,230
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:32,150
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:33,540
And I just thought,

103
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,200
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:35,330 --> 00:02:36,880
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:38,910
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:39,820
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:41,340
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:43,200
And when I found one,

109
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,090
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:45,090 --> 00:02:46,500
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:48,080
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,710
out and went looking.

113
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:51,230
Not for a product.

114
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,570
For an explanation.

115
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:54,550
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:56,670
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:59,250
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,260
And that's when I found

119
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:02,050
a video from a physical
therapist

120
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:02,540
named Dr.

121
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:04,590
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

122
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:06,500
had been through exactly
this.

123
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:08,810
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:08,810 --> 00:03:10,490
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,900
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:13,910
The ice.

127
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:15,460
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,420
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,550
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:20,900
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:23,270
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,360
It's a preview.

133
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,630
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:27,050
you this works fast.

135
00:03:27,090 --> 00:03:28,030
It doesn't.

136
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,120
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:30,850
and to look at what's

138
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:32,150
going on around your new
knee

139
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:33,750
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,820
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:37,640
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,580
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,010
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:41,010 --> 00:03:42,230
everything for me.

145
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:44,260
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:46,040
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,790
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

148
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:49,160
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,220
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,820
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:53,030 --> 00:03:54,390
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:56,040
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,380
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,230
He said,

155
00:03:58,230 --> 00:03:59,910
think about a swollen foot

156
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:01,030
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:01,610 --> 00:04:02,880
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:05,220
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:06,650
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:08,060
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:09,150
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:10,660
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,510
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:14,560
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,180
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:18,910
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,740
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:22,420
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,160
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,060
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:28,960
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:30,380
So when you bend,

173
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:32,130
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:33,480
When you straighten,

175
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,760
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:36,210
That's the band.

177
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:38,600
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:39,630
And you start being

179
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:40,750
the one who says,

180
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:41,570
you go ahead.

181
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:42,790
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:44,810
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:44,810 --> 00:04:46,980
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:47,210 --> 00:04:49,350
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:49,350 --> 00:04:50,370
around the knee.

186
00:04:50,410 --> 00:04:51,410
Worth doing,

187
00:04:51,410 --> 00:04:52,320
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,760
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,940
taking up room.

190
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:56,550
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:56,550 --> 00:04:58,760
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:04:59,030 --> 00:05:01,020
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,760
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,360
finally calms down,

195
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,820
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:07,310
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:08,820
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,840
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:10,970 --> 00:05:12,850
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:14,640
After two years of this,

201
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:16,230
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,570
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,620
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:22,400
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,870
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:25,050 --> 00:05:26,120
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,890
compression braces,
creams,

208
00:05:27,890 --> 00:05:29,430
half of Amazon really,

209
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:31,220
and all any of it gave me

210
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:32,100
was an hour.

211
00:05:32,150 --> 00:05:33,070
I even looked at going

212
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:34,930
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,890
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:36,890 --> 00:05:39,150
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:40,540
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:41,910
Then one night I went

217
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:43,280
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,120
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:46,590
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:46,590 --> 00:05:48,370
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:50,960
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,370
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:54,580
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,420
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:58,000
This one device,

226
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,480
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,830
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:03,870
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:03,870 --> 00:06:05,230
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:06,680
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,450
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:08,590 --> 00:06:10,460
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:12,840
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,870
that if I ever found

235
00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:15,270
something that helped,

236
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:16,320
I'd say so.

237
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:18,300
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:19,830
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:22,130
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:22,450 --> 00:06:23,800
It looked like the cheap

241
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,410
knee sleeves off Amazon

242
00:06:26,410 --> 00:06:28,100
that did nothing for me.

243
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:30,600
But I went to their
website anyway,

244
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,760
just to see what all

245
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,020
the fuss was about.

246
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:35,180
It's the same red light
therapy

247
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,230
clinics charge $200 a
session

248
00:06:38,230 --> 00:06:40,460
for, off machines that
cost

249
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:42,230
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:42,230 --> 00:06:43,570
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:44,920
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:47,230
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:49,710
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:52,280
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,630
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:56,550
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:58,710
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:06:58,930 --> 00:07:00,700
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:02,100
Ninety days.

260
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,990
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:06,310
no questions, no store
credit,

262
00:07:06,310 --> 00:07:08,130
and you don't even send it
back.

263
00:07:08,430 --> 00:07:10,790
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

264
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:12,410
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:13,930
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:13,930 --> 00:07:14,890
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,240
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:18,630
Only the right knee was
replaced,

269
00:07:18,630 --> 00:07:20,680
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

270
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,720
and I'd done it for two
years.

271
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:25,180
The left one was carrying
the difference.

272
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:25,800
When it came,

273
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,990
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

274
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:29,190
because I'd been let down
too

275
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:30,780
many times to get excited.

276
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:32,440
What I felt was warmth.

277
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,370
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

278
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,540
More like it was coming
from inside

279
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:38,690
the knee and spreading
around it.

280
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,980
And that was it.

281
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,680
That was the whole
experience.

282
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:42,950
When I took it off,

283
00:07:42,950 --> 00:07:43,850
I'll be honest,

284
00:07:43,850 --> 00:07:45,540
nothing dramatic had
happened.

285
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:47,400
And after what that video
said,

286
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,540
that's exactly what I
expected.

287
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:50,310
What was different

288
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:51,280
was that for the first

289
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,380
time in two years

290
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:53,720
I'd done something for my
knee

291
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,760
instead of to it.

292
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,250
Twenty minutes,

293
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:57,410
in my own chair.

294
00:07:57,450 --> 00:07:59,440
No drive, no copay.

295
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,510
They say twenty minutes.

296
00:08:01,730 --> 00:08:02,820
I did thirty,

297
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:04,090
twice a day,

298
00:08:04,090 --> 00:08:06,010
lowest setting that first
week.

299
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:07,710
I put it on the calendar.

300
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,490
The first week,

301
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:09,340
I couldn't have told

302
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:10,960
you if anything was
happening.

303
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,050
I tried not to get

304
00:08:12,050 --> 00:08:12,720
my hopes up.

305
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,150
I'd had things help for a
week

306
00:08:14,150 --> 00:08:15,080
and then stop.

307
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,490
But somewhere in the
second week

308
00:08:16,490 --> 00:08:17,580
I noticed I'd come down

309
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,370
the stairs without holding
the rail.

310
00:08:19,490 --> 00:08:20,690
I hadn't decided to.

311
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:21,980
I just did it,

312
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:23,640
then stopped halfway down

313
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:24,940
because I realized.

314
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:26,730
By the end of the fourth
week

315
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:27,840
I'd slept through the
night

316
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,210
four times running.

317
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:30,660
I stood at the counter

318
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:31,890
and finished making dinner

319
00:08:31,890 --> 00:08:33,500
without looking for the
stool.

320
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:35,450
None of that is dramatic.

321
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:36,440
All of it was gone

322
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,590
for two years.

323
00:08:37,770 --> 00:08:39,410
A few weeks later my wife
asked

324
00:08:39,410 --> 00:08:40,360
if I wanted to walk

325
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,150
the long way around the
block.

326
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,600
And for the first time

327
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,410
in two years,

328
00:08:44,410 --> 00:08:45,580
I said yes.

329
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,610
I wanted to understand
why,

330
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,150
so I read the whole thing.

331
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,970
It comes down to four
steps.

332
00:08:51,010 --> 00:08:51,690
One.

333
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,730
The tissue around a new
knee can

334
00:08:53,730 --> 00:08:56,650
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

335
00:08:57,010 --> 00:08:57,710
Two.

336
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,470
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

337
00:09:00,470 --> 00:09:01,510
so it takes up more

338
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:02,740
room than it should.

339
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:03,740
Three.

340
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,560
There's only so much room
in there.

341
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,140
Bending compresses it.

342
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,950
Straightening pulls it
tight.

343
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:10,660
That's the squeeze.

344
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,450
Four.

345
00:09:11,730 --> 00:09:14,040
Red and near-infrared
light have been

346
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:16,280
studied for calming that
inflammation,

347
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:17,610
so the swelling and the
pressure

348
00:09:17,610 --> 00:09:18,830
can come down with it.

349
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,050
In a randomized trial,

350
00:09:20,050 --> 00:09:21,630
patients given light
therapy after

351
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:22,410
a knee replacement

352
00:09:22,410 --> 00:09:23,160
had less pain,

353
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,110
less swelling

354
00:09:24,110 --> 00:09:25,710
and better early movement
than

355
00:09:25,710 --> 00:09:26,620
those who weren't.

356
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,440
A 2025 review said the
same,

357
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,600
and was clear the evidence

358
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:31,580
is still limited.

359
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:34,000
I probably sound like a
broken record

360
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,420
to the people I work with.

361
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,500
But after two years of
doing everything

362
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,370
I was told and getting
nowhere,

363
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:40,710
you have no idea what it's

364
00:09:40,710 --> 00:09:42,300
like to sleep through the
night,

365
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:43,580
say yes to the walk,

366
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,020
and get my life back.

367
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:46,590
So take it from me.

368
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,970
Don't spend another year
waiting

369
00:09:47,970 --> 00:09:49,020
for it to settle.

370
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,750
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

371
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:52,500
More than ten thousand
people

372
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,640
with pain after a knee

373
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:56,370
replacement have already
tried this.

374
00:09:56,550 --> 00:09:58,100
Some had it worse than I
did.

375
00:09:58,410 --> 00:09:59,550
You can get the KenRelief

376
00:09:59,550 --> 00:10:01,190
wrap from their website,

377
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:02,770
with a discount link

378
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:04,550
and ninety days to try it.

379
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:06,680
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

380
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:07,720
you get your money back

381
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,920
and you keep the wrap.

382
00:10:09,110 --> 00:10:10,290
They only release so many

383
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:11,380
at that price.

384
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,860
If it's still there,

385
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:13,780
